From 573ef372424c8008ab52d96cbfe4279a10018b3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kissshot <ttyinzg@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:32:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(trajectory): continue a branch under a new
 instruction

Branching from a trajectory record forked and opened the child, then left
the user to retype their intent. The row control now opens a dialog with an
optional instruction, so one gesture forks and continues.

The instruction is trimmed and submitted to the child as an ordinary queued
prompt: a freshly forked child is idle, while steering exists to interrupt a
turn already running. An empty or whitespace-only field branches without
continuing.

Failure never discards work. A refused fork reports failure and leaves this
trajectory untouched. A refused instruction keeps the already-opened branch
and reports failure rather than unwinding it, and the dialog stays open with
the typed text so it can be resubmitted or copied out.
